{"author":{"id":"836d943203cf5a4f01ab5d4b4780de84949c43734f2256a167cc5931ae5d8c66"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794180726,"nonce":"FOd7Wd5NKXBtQn3s8aRV4R2OHeY=","title":"L7 — New issue dialog (bug, task, epic) backed by git-bug","message":"## Context\nThe \"New Bug\" pill sends `Message::Noop` (`src/ui/screen.rs:81`). Writes exist for close, reopen, state and comment (`src/gitbug/write.rs:134-175`) and are serialized per repo by `WriteQueue` (`src/writes.rs:48`), but nothing creates issues.\n\n## Files\n- `src/gitbug/write.rs` — new `create(root, kind, title, body, epic) -\u003e Result\u003cIssueDetail, GitBugError\u003e`; follow `comment` (`write.rs:153`): `--message=` (never `-F`), `--non-interactive`, full-id resolution\n- `src/app.rs` — `NewIssue` form state and messages; queue through `WriteQueue`, then reload that repo through the existing load path\n- `src/ui/new_issue.rs` — new modal using the `done::overlay` pattern\n\n## Approach\n- `git bug bug new --title=\u003ct\u003e --message=\u003cbody\u003e --non-interactive`, then read the new id from the output and add the labels `kind:\u003ckind\u003e`, plus `epic:\u003cfull-id\u003e` for a task or bug with a parent epic, in one `bug label new` call\n- Form fields: repo (defaults to the current repo filter, else the first repo), kind (Bug by default from the top bar), title (required), body (`text_editor`), parent epic (`pick_list` of open epics in that repo; hidden for epics)\n- Submitting shows a spinner on the button. On success: close, select the new issue in Issues, and push a notification (L6). On error: show it inline and keep the form.\n- Cmd+N opens it (add to `keymap.rs` from L5)\n\n## Depends on\nL6 — the notifications list; L5 — the keymap\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Unit tests for the argument builders (`create` plan) in the style of the existing `write.rs` tests (`write.rs:290-360`): a task with an epic gets `kind:task` and `epic:\u003cfull-id\u003e`; an epic gets only `kind:epic`; an empty title is rejected before any CLI call\n- The UI stays responsive while creating; the new issue appears in the list without a manual rescan\n- Gates pass","files":null}]}